# Normalise line endings on every platform.
#
# This is a correctness requirement, not a style preference. The evidence
# register hashes files on disk and compares them against the SHA-256 baselines
# in data/evidence_manifest.json. If a Windows checkout produced CRLF while
# Linux produced LF, the same committed file would hash differently on the two
# platforms and the custody check would report ALTERED for an untouched file.
# Pinning the working-tree ending to LF keeps those baselines valid everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf
